# Shipyard code owners. Replace @OWNER with the maintainers (a user or a team) who may approve changes to the
# framework and to its notes. The rulesets require a code-owner review on the default branch.

# Shipyard's working notes: never on a work branch, and never changed without a human.
/.ai/                          @OWNER

# The framework itself: agents, skills, hooks, workflows, prompts and the tool-independent core. Code review
# and the cloud agent read these from the pull request's head branch, so a change here changes the reviewers.
/.github/agents/               @OWNER
/.github/skills/               @OWNER
/.github/hooks/                @OWNER
/.github/extensions/           @OWNER
/.github/prompts/              @OWNER
/.github/instructions/         @OWNER
/.github/workflows/            @OWNER
/.github/rulesets/             @OWNER
/.github/copilot-instructions.md @OWNER
/AGENTS.md                     @OWNER
/shipyard/                     @OWNER
